<%
  /*
   * The account half of "Build your profile": sign-in details, roles, password, LinkedIn and
   * the data rights. It used to be its own page (/profile/settings); it is now the last
   * section of the profile page, and the ONLY section an account without the consultant role
   * sees. Every form in it is its own <form>, so this partial must never be rendered inside
   * the profile form — the browser drops nested forms silently.
   */
%>
<section class="profile-section mb-3" id="account" data-tab="account">
  <h2 class="h5 mb-3">Account</h2>
  <% if (!user.email_verified) { %>
    <div class="alert alert-warning d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2">
      <span>Your email address is not confirmed yet.</span>
      <form method="post" action="/auth/resend-verification" class="ms-auto">
        <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
        <button class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary" type="submit">Resend confirmation</button>
      </form>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="glass-card mb-4">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3 class="h6 mb-3">Sign-in details</h3>
          <dl class="row mb-0 small">
            <dt class="col-5 text-muted-2">Email</dt><dd class="col-7"><%= user.email %></dd>
            <dt class="col-5 text-muted-2">Member since</dt><dd class="col-7"><%= new Date(user.created_at).toISOString().slice(0, 10) %></dd>
            <dt class="col-5 text-muted-2">Primary role</dt><dd class="col-7"><%= user.user_type %></dd>
            <% if (user.terms_version) { %>
              <dt class="col-5 text-muted-2">Terms accepted</dt>
              <dd class="col-7">v<%= user.terms_version %> on <%= new Date(user.terms_accepted_at).toISOString().slice(0, 10) %></dd>
            <% } %>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="glass-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="h6 mb-3" id="roles">What you use the Hub for</h2>
          <form method="post" action="/profile/settings/roles">
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
            <%
              /*
               * Without the consultant role this page already leads with "Set up my consultant
               * profile", which adds exactly that role. A second checkbox doing the same thing
               * a screen lower is two controls for one decision, so it appears only once the
               * role is held — as a disabled, ticked record of it.
               */
            %>
            <% if (user.is_consultant) { %>
              <div class="form-check">
                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="r-consultant" checked disabled>
                <label class="form-check-label" for="r-consultant">Find work as a consultant</label>
              </div>
            <% } %>
            <div class="form-check">
              <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="roles" value="company" id="r-company"
                     <%= user.is_company ? 'checked disabled' : '' %>>
              <label class="form-check-label" for="r-company">Hire Salesforce talent</label>
            </div>
            <div class="form-check mb-3">
              <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="roles" value="recruiter" id="r-recruiter"
                     <%= user.is_recruiter ? 'checked disabled' : '' %>>
              <label class="form-check-label" for="r-recruiter">Place candidates as an agency</label>
            </div>
            <%
              /*
               * A disabled checkbox posts nothing, so each held role is re-sent as a hidden
               * field. `addSelfServiceRoles` unions and never removes, so this is belt and
               * braces rather than load-bearing — but without it the form would look like it
               * was asking to drop a role it cannot drop.
               */
            %>
            <% if (user.is_consultant) { %><input type="hidden" name="roles" value="consultant"><% } %>
            <% if (user.is_company) { %><input type="hidden" name="roles" value="company"><% } %>
            <% if (user.is_recruiter) { %><input type="hidden" name="roles" value="recruiter"><% } %>
            <% if (!user.is_consultant) { %>
              <p class="form-text mb-1">To find work as a consultant, use <a href="#consultant-setup">Set up my consultant profile</a> above.</p>
            <% } %>
            <p class="form-text">
              Adding a role here is instant. Removing one is done by support, so a mis-click can
              never take away access you rely on.
            </p>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Save roles</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="glass-card">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="h6 mb-3">Change password</h2>
          <form method="post" action="/profile/settings/password">
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
            <div class="mb-3">
              <label class="form-label" for="current_password">Current password</label>
              <input class="form-control" id="current_password" name="current_password" type="password" required autocomplete="current-password">
            </div>
            <div class="mb-3">
              <label class="form-label" for="password">New password</label>
              <input class="form-control" id="password" name="password" type="password" required autocomplete="new-password">
              <p class="form-text">At least 8 characters, with upper case, lower case and a number.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="mb-3">
              <label class="form-label" for="confirm_password">Confirm new password</label>
              <input class="form-control" id="confirm_password" name="confirm_password" type="password" required autocomplete="new-password">
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Update password</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# Second pair of the same grid, so every card shares the same two column edges. %>
    <div class="col-lg-6" id="linkedin">
      <div class="glass-card h-100">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h2 class="h6 mb-1">LinkedIn</h2>

          <% if (linkedInIdentity) { %>
            <p class="mb-2">
              <span class="badge-hub ok"><i class="bi bi-patch-check"></i> LinkedIn confirmed</span>
              as <strong><%= linkedInIdentity.display_name || 'an unnamed account' %></strong>
              on <%= new Date(linkedInIdentity.verified_at).toLocaleDateString('en-GB') %>.
            </p>

            <% if (!linkedInIdentity.name_matched) { %>
              <div class="alert alert-warning">
                The name on that LinkedIn account does not match the name on your Hub profile.
                That is fine if both are yours — a middle name, a married name, a different
                spelling — but anyone reading your profile will see both, so it is worth making
                them agree if you can.
              </div>
            <% } %>

            <form method="post" action="/linkedin/disconnect">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
              <input type="hidden" name="redirectTo" value="/profile/settings#linkedin">
              <button class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" type="submit">Disconnect</button>
            </form>

          <% } else if (linkedInEnabled) { %>
            <p class="text-muted-2">
              Sign in to LinkedIn once and your profile carries a confirmation badge.
            </p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/linkedin/start?returnTo=%2Fprofile%2Fsettings%23linkedin">
              <i class="bi bi-linkedin"></i> Confirm with LinkedIn
            </a>
          <% } else { %>
            <p class="text-muted-2 mb-0">
              LinkedIn verification is not switched on for this deployment.
            </p>
          <% } %>

          <hr>
          <%
            /*
             * Said plainly, on the page, because a badge that implies more than it checked
             * is worse than no badge. LinkedIn's userinfo response carries the member's
             * name and nothing else usable — no vanity URL, no headline, no positions —
             * so this is the full extent of what the badge can honestly mean.
             */
          %>
          <h3 class="h6">What this badge means, exactly</h3>
          <ul class="small text-muted-2 mb-0">
            <li><strong>It confirms</strong> that you control a LinkedIn account, and the name on it.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>It does not confirm</strong> the LinkedIn link on your consultant profile,
              your job title, your employer or your experience. LinkedIn does not make any of
              those available, so nothing here could check them.
            </li>
            <li>
              We ask only for your name and email, and we store your name and an opaque account
              identifier. <strong>No access token is kept</strong> — this site never posts
              anything to LinkedIn and has no way to.
            </li>
            <li>
              One LinkedIn account can confirm one Hub account. Disconnecting removes the badge
              immediately.
            </li>
            <li>
              LinkedIn is <strong>not a way to sign in</strong> here. It only ever links to an
              account you are already signed in to.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-lg-6">
    <div class="glass-card h-100"><div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="h6 mb-3">Your data</h2>
      <p class="small text-muted-2">
        Both of these are yours to do, now, without asking anybody. A right you have to
        request is a right somebody can be slow about.
      </p>
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" href="/profile/data">Download everything held about you</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm" href="/profile/close">Close your account</a>
      </div>
      <div class="form-text mt-2">
        The download is a JSON file, generated on the spot and never stored. Closing your
        account explains exactly what is destroyed and the few things that stay, with the
        reason for each, before you confirm anything.
      </div>
    </div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
